# Contributing to [[ name ]]

## Development setup

```sh
pip install -e .[dev]
pytest
```

## Commit messages

Commits follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org): `type(scope): description`,
with types such as `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor` and `test`. Releases are automatic: a `feat`
releases a minor version, a `fix` a patch, and a breaking change (`type!:` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:`
footer) a major one.

To force a particular release, put a directive alone on a line in the commit body:
`+:major`, `+:minor`, `+:patch`, or `+:rc` / `+:pre` / `+:prepre` for a pre-release.

## Pull requests

Keep each pull request to one change, with a Conventional Commit title and passing checks. Describe
what changed and why in the pull request itself.
